JWasm: -Zj makes no "far call optimisation"

For a CALL to a FAR procedure in the current segment (or another segment
of its group), JWasm emits PUSH CS and a near CALL, as MASM 6 does.
MASM 5 emits the far CALL (9A), one byte longer. Under -Zj, a CALL to a
FAR label in the current segment is far, and one to a FAR label elsewhere
is left far.

Needed for the message retriever (MSGSERV.ASM) in ATTRIB and MEM, whose
_MSGRET.ASM calls SYSLOADMSG, SYSGETMSG and SYSDISPMSG, FAR procedures
defined earlier in the same segment.

diff --git a/src/branch.c b/src/branch.c
index 79b71ad..6f6e6ca 100644
--- a/src/branch.c
